# Copy to .env, fill in values, then pass extract --env-file .env explicitly.
# Plain KEY=value data only: no PowerShell $env:, Read-Host, or Markdown links.
# Command-line options > existing process environment > this file.
ATTESTEXTRACT_BASE_URL=https://your-provider.example/v1
ATTESTEXTRACT_MODEL=your-model-name
ATTESTEXTRACT_API_KEY=replace-with-your-key

# Minimal selection: --model-id deepseek:deepseek-flash or qwen:qwen3.8-27b.
# Configure the corresponding key once; these selectors ignore ATTESTEXTRACT_*.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=replace-with-your-deepseek-key
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=replace-with-your-beijing-key
# Optional Qwen key aliases, selected by presence: QWEN_API_KEY > DASHSCOPE_API_KEY > VLM_API_KEY.
# Leave unused aliases absent; an empty selected variable is an error, not a fallback.
# QWEN_API_KEY=replace-with-your-beijing-key
# VLM_API_KEY=replace-with-your-beijing-key
# Optional Beijing workspace URL: QWEN_BASE_URL with QWEN_API_KEY or DASHSCOPE_API_KEY;
# VLM_BASE_URL with VLM_API_KEY. Omit to use the Beijing public compatible endpoint.
# Native model IDs in DEEPSEEK_MODEL / VLM_MODEL do not override --model-id.
# Advanced or custom routes can use named profiles in examples/backends.toml.
